# Controls what `gcloud builds submit backend` uploads to Cloud Build. WITHOUT this
# file, gcloud does NOT automatically pick up backend/.dockerignore's rules — it looks
# for a .gcloudignore (or, as a fallback, a .gitignore) IN THE SUBMITTED DIRECTORY
# (backend/), and neither existed here. Result: the entire backend/.venv/ (torch,
# transformers, ~55k files, ~6GB) got archived and uploaded on every deploy. Mirrors
# backend/.dockerignore's intent exactly.
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
tests/
*.md
.env
.env.*
